{"id": "EUVD-2026-35147", "enisaUuid": "2fc889e8-fe37-35cf-b100-50f068321e4c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: frequency: admv1013: fix NULL pointer dereference on str\n\nWhen device_property_read_string() fails, str is left uninitialized\nbut the code falls through to strcmp(str, ...), dereferencing a garbage\npointer. Replace manual read/strcmp with\ndevice_property_match_property_string() and consolidate the SE mode\nenums into a single sequential enum, mapping to hardware register\nvalues via a switch consistent with other bitfields in the driver.\n\nSeveral cleanup patches have been applied to this driver recently so\nthis will need a manual backport.", "datePublished": "2026-06-08T15:41:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:41:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ef8b71a0fc692f8cb7f124a8143b540446b1fe9d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a9d8ec2051c2d80158ed7bded5e158c42870037", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5e9f1bad26df3d3afb3cbbfa408b6d6e809708ac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2dc8d26690bf4e7226409563221c37bc095c94ff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aac0a51b16700b403a55b67ba495de021db78763"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-46282", "GHSA-qrv5-4j39-f7c6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00c85e32-7c4f-374e-8cd0-9125b1555745", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "0f4dd03d-f788-32d6-be30-0fdff36e2ddc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "da35a7b526d9b258a2cb8b7816f736a41b32176b <5e9f1bad26df3d3afb3cbbfa408b6d6e809708ac"}, {"id": "16e84002-ef7b-3bff-922a-53cb433fdc73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "555a5a40-ebed-3678-a94e-53c2b8410e37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.86"}, {"id": "6f6855b7-0fba-3fb9-9726-30eb307